  "rdfs:comment": [
    "Ownership transfer chain: shipping, receiving, and retail sale of a serialized device.",
    "Architecture: the event references identifiers by URI — GTIN in epcList, GLN in readPoint/bizLocation, party GLN in source/destination. Model-, location-, and party-level master data is served by the GS1 Digital Link / Web Vocabulary resolver when those URIs are dereferenced; it is NOT embedded in the event.",
    "masterDataAvailableFor carries ONLY item/lot-level master data (e.g. countryOfOrigin, regulatoryInformation, harvestDate, EUDR plot geolocation). ilmd carries lot/instance data of the items this event creates. Observation extensions sit at event level.",
    "",
    "HTTP header: GS1-Extensions: oec=https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/,euelec=https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/eu/electronics/",
    "Warranty and purchase country are deliberately NOT event extensions here: the retail_selling eventTime is the warranty start, the warranty terms (gs1:manufacturersWarranty / gs1:WarrantyPromise with gs1:durationOfWarranty) are model-level master data, and the country of purchase is location-level master data of the store GLN in readPoint/bizLocation. All three are resolver-served.",
    "See: extensions/common/core/docs/EPCIS_MASTERDATA_AND_EXTENSIONS.md",
    "GS1 demo prefix 952 (7-digit GCP: 9521234)."
  ],
